+  hacks keep the game code of the game they are made from, and every HeartGold-based ROM used to
+  share `heartgold.sav`. The save state goes with the save (`Heartfelt Gold.sav.state`). Saves from
+  before carry on: the first time one of a game's ROMs starts, the old shared save is copied for
+  each ROM of that game, and the old file kept as a backup (`heartgold.sav.bak`); a ROM named like
+  it (`HeartGold.nds`, or a `rom.nds`) goes on using it. The other languages' saves
+  (`heartgold-fr.sav`, `black2-es.sav` ...) are handed on the same way. On the Switch, the older
+  one-game downloads' folders keep the game's save name.
+- **Every ROM has its own cheats too, named after the ROM file** (`Heartfelt Gold.nds` reads
+  `cheats/Heartfelt Gold.txt` and `Heartfelt Gold.mch`; which are on, the POPULAR CHEATS among
+  them, is kept in `Heartfelt Gold-on.txt`), the way saves are: cheats were kept by the game's
+  code (`IPKE.txt`), so every HeartGold-based ROM could turn on the same codes, made for only one
+  of them. The cheat database, `usrcheat.dat`, is used for a ROM only when it has an entry made
+  for that ROM (by its header), where it used to give a hack the first entry of the game's code.
