+To carry on a game from another emulator, put its .sav file in the saves folder named like your
+ROM (for example saves/Platinum (USA).sav for roms/Platinum (USA).nds). Back your saves up
+before you do. Saves used to be named after the game (black2.sav, heartgold.sav ...), one
+shared by every ROM of it: the first time one of them starts, that save is copied for each
+of the game's ROMs and the old file kept as a backup (heartgold.sav.bak); a ROM named like it
+(HeartGold.nds) just goes on using it.
+
+Cheats are kept the same way: the codes for a ROM go in a text file named like it (for example
+cheats/Heartfelt Gold.txt for roms/Heartfelt Gold.nds), so a game's hacks don't share them. Files
+named after the game's code (IPKE.txt), which every ROM of the game used to read, are not read any
+more: rename one after the ROM it is for (game.log says when one is left).
 
 
